{"body":"Users currently have no way to say whether a reply was good. This ticket: thumbs up/down on assistant messages, which \"weights\" (adjusts confidence in) the selected model's fit for the metrics collected per message (issue #17 — dependency).\n\nSuggested approach:\n- API: `POST /api/messages/:messageId/feedback` with `{ value: 'up' | 'down' }`, authenticated, idempotent (revote just overwrites); persists on the message document alongside its `metrics` from #17.\n- Frontend: thumbs up/down pair under each assistant message, subtle pending/opt-out lift, already-visible messages get the controls too.\n- Weighting model: keep a `modelMetricsStats` store (Mongo collection) of per-(modelName, metric-band) counts → up/down tallies, e.g. `llama-3.3-70b + high-technical + long prompt → 12↑/3↓`. When the router scores candidate models for a message, factor these empirical fit scores in alongside the existing complexity heuristics.\n- Cold start: fall back to neutral weight until a minimum sample count per band.\n- Feeding the router: this complements the online router, not replaces it; log the applied weight in the routing reason so LangSmith (#5) can surface it.\n- Acceptance: feedback round-trips for authed users (401 for others); thumbs show their current state after reload; router decisions demonstrably shift with accumulated feedback (covered by a test seeding stats and asserting a different model choice).","comments":[],"title":"Thumbs up/down feedback that weights model-vs-metrics fit"}
